**Read:** [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC), the complete primary-energy/emissions allocation assignment and relevant lectures; [Engineering Thermodynamics — Olivier Cleynen](../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ), cycle energy and useful-output accounting; [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), heat-exchanger and phase-change chapters.

Heating at one temperature level cannot automatically replace a different thermal service. Draw the hot and cold process temperature profiles, duties, timing and minimum approach conditions before proposing heat recovery. Include pressure loss, contamination separation, fouling and intermittent availability.

For cogeneration, report both useful heat and useful work, with explicit treatment of primary input and allocation. For storage, track energy, temperature range, losses, charge/discharge power, cycling and the state in which energy can be recovered. Sensible, latent and chemical storage require different state models.

Complete the actual allocation problem in [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC) and independently compare at least two service arrangements. Avoid counting the same recovered heat twice or assigning all energy the same ability to perform work. Full utility networks and storage manufacture remain deeper engineering routes connected through [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../../../engineering/electrical-power-engineering/Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ), [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618) and [Hephaestus](../../../Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001).

